# Cloudflare Pages headers. Replaces the [[headers]] blocks that used to live in
# netlify.toml — that file was inert here, which is why X-Frame-Options was silently
# missing from the live site while the other two happened to be set Cloudflare-side.
# Syntax: a path pattern, then indented "Header: value" lines.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Deliberately NOT immutable/max-age=1y. These filenames carry no content hash —
# assets/script.js and assets/style.css keep their names across edits — so a year-long
# immutable cache would pin returning visitors to whatever version they first loaded,
# with no way to push a fix. (netlify.toml declared exactly that rule, but it was inert
# on Cloudflare, so nothing was broken until these headers started applying for real.)
# An hour with revalidation still spares repeat visitors the ~10MB hero video re-fetch.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate
